    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> dhil created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/13996#discussion_r3666756815\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This is the interesting change introduced by this patch. It implements the WAST directive <code>assert_suspension</code>. I am not sure this is the best way to implement it.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 613225654,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1785251600
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> cfallin submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/13996#pullrequestreview-4798909716\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 613227109,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1785251991
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> cfallin created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/13996#discussion_r3666811503\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Rather than match on an error message, could we try to downcast the trap (see e.g. the <code>assert_exception</code> case above)?</p>\n<p>I see at least <a href=\"https://docs.rs/wasmtime/latest/wasmtime/enum.Trap.html#variant.UnhandledTag\"><code>UnhandledTag</code></a>; a quick skim didn't find the suspend-outside-cont but I guess you'd know what kind of trap that raises (and we can add a variant if it is not distinguished currently).</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 613227110,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1785251992
