        "timestamp": 1785256821
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> dhil created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/13996#discussion_r3667475480\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Fixed in <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/13996/commits/73b99fcffa49462d16724e2fdd98b8c4a049ba92\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/13996/commits/73b99fcffa49462d16724e2fdd98b8c4a049ba92</a>. Thanks! </p>\n<p>I realised that we map unhandled suspension and suspension outside a continuation to the same trap <code>UnhandledTag</code>. I think the difference only manifests in the spec interpreter's testsuite, meaning I think we can freely ignore the distinction here.</p>\n</blockquote>",
